  "query_preview": "..As a 500 mb low pushes south of AZ through the \nweekend, skies are becoming clear and the pressure gradient will \nstrengthen. This will create breezy conditions today that start to enhance\nsome drying of still saturated soils. Winds will be out of the \nnorth to northeast around 5-15 mph in most areas with gusts to \n20-35 mph along and south/southwest of the higher terrain. \n\nMonday through Thursday, a mostly dry and mild weather pattern is\nexpected. A weak short-wave trough is expected to cross through \nsouthern Arizona on Tuesday, but moisture will be very limited and\nis unlikely that more than an isolated shower or two will \ndevelop, mainly near the White Mountains. Looking further into the\nweekend, ensemble models continue to show a deepening west coast \ntrough that becomes a cut-off low as it moves over the United \nStates. Most models continue to favor a track that keeps the low \nsufficiently south to limit moisture returns into the region. \nHowever, a shift northward could bring another round of showers to\nour area by Friday.",
